## LPDDR5 command-bus testbed, DDR4 SO-DIMM form factor, for the ZCU104 PL socket J1
## Host: ZCU104 rev 1.0, XCZU7EV-2FFVC1156, socket J1 (HP banks 64 / 65 / 66 at 1.2 V).  Part xczu7ev-ffvc1156-2-e.
##
## Port names: a differential port <x>_p is the FPGA P pin of its I/O pair, whatever leg of the card it carries.
## Pairs whose true leg (_t) sits on the FPGA N pin are marked INVERTED; the polarity is also in
## lpddr5_testbed_pins.vh (CK_INVERTED / WCK_INVERTED / RDQS_INVERTED).
## Comment fields: finger (card side) | card net -> DRAM ball | bank, nibble, N index (bitslice in the nibble) | pin name
##
## Banks 64 / 65 / 66 are HP banks at VCCO = 1.2 V on the ZCU104 (fixed by the board).  No INTERNAL_VREF and no
## DCI_CASCADE constraint is needed (no VREF-referenced input and no DCI output in this file).

